.TH TOOLS9P 8
.SH NAME
tools9p \- serve a restricted Veltro tool and capability namespace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tools9p
[
.B -DvN
]
[
.B -P
.I profile
]
[
.B -a
.I activity
]
[
.B -m
.I mountpoint
]
[
.B -p
.I path[:ro|:rw]
]
.I tool ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tools9p
serves the active Veltro tools and their effective namespace capabilities at
.BR /tool .
Only named tools exist. Each invocation receives a namespace constructed by
.IR nsconstruct .
.PP
Production profile declarations are directories below
.BR /lib/veltro/profiles .
Their scalar-file shape matches the read-only audit surface served at
.BR /tool :
.PP
.nf
	tools
	paths
	meta/role
	meta/nodevs
	meta/xenith
	meta/actid
	walletbudget        optional
.fi
.PP
Use
.B -P
to materialize a profile. The option may be repeated; tools and paths form an
additive union, while conflicting permissions or wallet budgets are errors.
.PP
The effective paths file uses records of the form
.IR "path ro|rw|cow" .
Activity scratch is always
.B /tmp/veltro/scratch cow
and is constructed specially. Passing that path with
.B -p
does not recursively grant or stage it.
.PP
A non-empty
.B /tool/walletbudget
is returned only when the dispatcher is enforcing that positive uint256,
currency-specific aggregate limit before wallet tool dispatch. Budgeted
profiles reject unmetered payment tools.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -P " profile"
Load a canonical runtime profile. Repeat for additive composition.
.TP
.B -N
Declare the NODEVS agent profile.
.TP
.BI -a " activity"
Set the activity identity used for scratch and staged writes.
.TP
.BI -m " mountpoint"
Serve somewhere other than
.BR /tool .
.TP
.BI -p " path[:ro|:rw]"
Add an ordinary filesystem capability. Repeat as needed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
	tools9p -P profile-minimal-headless
	tools9p -P profile-desktop-gui -P profile-messaging
	nsaudit -m /tool
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /lib/veltro/profiles
Canonical production profile declarations.
.TP
.B /tmp/veltro/.ns/manifest
Effective restricted namespace manifest, sealed into the audit chain when
auditing is enabled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR nsaudit (1),
.IR namespace (6)
